    "problem": "Which of the following gives the length of the curve defined by the parametric equations\n$$\n\\displaystyle x = t^{2} + 1, y = t^{3} + 2t\n$$\nfrom $t =-1$ to $t = 1$?",
    "worked_solution": "Differentiate: $x'=2t$ and $y'=3t^2+2$. Thus $$(x')^2+(y')^2=4t^2+(3t^2+2)^2=9t^4+16t^2+4.$$ Therefore $$L=\\int_{-1}^1\\sqrt{9t^4+16t^2+4}\\,dt.$$",
